## Missing analytic lemma: tight bounds on -γ - log π

The Omega anchor value is `-γ - log π + Σ step22OmegaArchWeightReSeriesTerm (1/20) n`,
so tight bounds on the transcendental constant `-γ - log π` are required.
The target anchor interval has width ~2e-77, so the bounds must be
correspondingly tight.

Proof route (not yet formalised):
- Use `Real.eulerMascheroniSeq_lt_eulerMascheroniConstant` at large N
  for a lower bound on γ, and `eulerMascheroniConstant_lt_eulerMascheroniSeq'`
  for an upper bound.  Both require `harmonic(N)` (exact rational) and
  `log(N)` / `log(N+1)` bounds.
- Bound `log(N)` using `Real.le_log_iff_exp_le` / `Real.log_lt_iff_lt_exp`
  combined with Taylor-remainder bounds on `exp` from
  `Real.sum_le_exp_of_nonneg` and `Real.exp_bound'`.
- Bound `log π` similarly, using `Real.pi_gt_d20` and `Real.pi_lt_d20`
  for 20-digit π bounds.
-/

